<title>USA: Maine group urges state to lower property taxes.</title>
<headline>Maine group urges state to lower property taxes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maine Municipal Association wants to raise statewide taxes to lower the property tax, and spelled out is plan before the legislature's taxation committee.</p>
<p>The group would broaden the sales tax to cover amusements and some services. The money would be used to fund a property tax exemption for part of the value of Maine citizens' residences.</p>
<p>The group also wants to remove the property tax exemption many non-profit organizations now enjoy. Lawmakers gave the plan a polite hearing, but raised more questions than the group could answer about how it would work.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
